From fcddf063c9069fd4418dc4affeed5df0f07f0b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: captainbeo <captainbeo@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:04:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(kiro): guard parseEventStreamTracked against
 mid-frame idle stalls

io.ReadFull blocks indefinitely when the upstream stops sending data
mid-frame. For callers with their own request timeouts (e.g. gateway's
StreamingTimeout), this is bounded, but a caller without one could hang
forever.

Wrap resp.Body in an idleTimeoutReader that cancels the request context
after 5 minutes of read inactivity. The reader checks ctx.Err() before
blocking, causing io.ReadFull to unblock and return context.Canceled.

Also removed Client.Timeout from GetClientForProxy (was still 5m), which
would abort healthy streams after 5 minutes total. Long Claude Opus
answers often exceed 5 minutes.

Fixes: lines 568+589 in proxy/kiro.go (parseEventStreamTracked).
Tests: proxy/idle_timeout_reader_test.go covers timeout+reset+EOF+Close.
